---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {stylesheet} from '../../../data/assets.js';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Hero and animated gradients" current="hero" documentation cssCustomizer={false}>
  <Fragment slot="head">{['reva.hero.css','reva.gradients.css'].map(file=><link rel="stylesheet" href={stylesheet(file)}/>)}</Fragment>
  <div class="hero-showcase">
    <header><p class="doc-kicker">NATIVE CSS · SOURCE PREVIEW</p><h1>Hero and gradient effects.</h1><p>Only the selected phrase changes colour. Background light and text stay independent; the letters and content remain still.</p><p><a href={base+'components/hero/'}>Hero markup</a> · <a href={base+'components/gradients/'}>Gradient effects and options</a></p></header>
    <p class="doc-note">Temporary colour test: the highlighted text uses purple/green in light mode and pink/cyan in dark mode. The original slow animation timing is unchanged.</p>
    <label class="pause-control"><input id="hero-pause" type="checkbox"/> Pause gradient animations</label>
    <section class="hero gradient-background" data-accent="violet" data-motion="subtle" aria-labelledby="hero-subtle-title">
      <h2 id="hero-subtle-title">Build <span class="gradient-text">something remarkable.</span></h2>
      <p>A selected phrase with gentle colour movement. Subtle motion takes 24 seconds in each direction.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#glass-hero-demo">Explore the glass hero</a>
    </section>
    <div class="hero-backdrop" id="glass-hero-demo">
      <section class="hero gradient-background" data-material="glass" data-theme="dark" data-accent="blue" data-motion="subtle" aria-labelledby="hero-glass-title">
        <h2 id="hero-glass-title">Let your ideas <span class="gradient-text">shine through.</span></h2>
        <p>Translucent moving colour leaves the frosted surface and its backdrop blur visible.</p>
        <a class="button" href="#hero-expressive-demo">Compare expressive motion</a>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="hero gradient-background" id="hero-expressive-demo" data-accent="orange" data-motion="expressive" aria-labelledby="hero-expressive-title">
      <header><h2 id="hero-expressive-title">A little more <span class="gradient-text">colour in motion.</span></h2><p>Expressive motion uses the same smooth effect over 12 seconds in each direction.</p><a class="button" href="#hero-static-demo">See the static version</a></header>
      <figure><img src={base+'images/example-landscape.svg'} width="640" height="360" alt="Illustrated hills beneath the sun"/></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="hero gradient-background" id="hero-static-demo" data-motion="none" data-theme="dark" aria-labelledby="hero-static-title">
      <h2 id="hero-static-title">Still <span class="gradient-text">full of colour.</span></h2><p>Motion none keeps the gradient static. Reduced motion also stops both effects automatically.</p><a class="button" href={base+'components/gradients/'}>Read the component guide</a>
    </section>
    <p>New source preview: visual/browser acceptance is pending. Check your selected colours against the actual background, especially custom photographs and translucent surfaces.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style is:global>
.hero-showcase { display:grid; gap:2rem; padding-block:2rem; }
/* Temporary demo-only endpoints: deliberately distant hues for mobile review. */
.hero-showcase .gradient-text {
  --re-gradient-text-start: light-dark(#8a0dc7, #ff70d2);
  --re-gradient-text-end: light-dark(#006b56, #46e8ff);
}
.hero-showcase > header { max-inline-size:65ch; }
.hero-backdrop { padding:clamp(.5rem,2vw,2rem); border-radius:var(--re-radius); background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 5% 10%,#173044,transparent 65%),radial-gradient(ellipse at 95% 90%,#342352,transparent 65%),#0c1220; }
.hero-showcase:has(#hero-pause:checked) .gradient-text,
.hero-showcase:has(#hero-pause:checked) .gradient-background::before { animation-play-state:paused; }
@media (forced-colors:active), print { .hero-backdrop { background:transparent; } }
</style>
